# Line endings.
#
# This repo is authored on Windows but its scripts must run on Linux too -- the
# shipped .devcontainer, WSL, and CI runners all execute them. A shell script
# committed with CRLF fails at exec time with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M",
# so these types are pinned to LF in the repository regardless of the author's
# core.autocrlf setting.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Windows-side helpers stay CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
*.bsa   binary
*.esp   binary
*.esm   binary
*.esl   binary
*.nif   binary
*.xwm   binary

# Extensionless test shims are shell scripts too. Without this they inherit the
# author's core.autocrlf and check out as CRLF, which dies on a Linux runner with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M" -- the exact failure the block above prevents
# for *.sh. Caught by a fresh-clone check, not in CI.
tests/bin/* text eol=lf
